https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BbYj3tJRSO8  (Capo 0)

The version in A is probably easier to play.

TIP:  This song has two key changes.  The first brings in the (C#) which is played like a (D/A) on the 1st fret.  (F#) is just (F) played up one fret, and (G#) is played like an (F) on the 4th fret.  The other key change isn't so bad.  If you don't want to deal with the key changes then you can just stay in (C) and play the same chords for all verses. 

TIP:  For the intro, strum the chord and pick the note (notes may or may not transpose).  For untransposed strum (C).  Play it 8 times (or 4 times if you consider it a couplet) then pick the 1st string (e), play (C) twice more and pick the covered 2nd string (c); play (C) twice more and begin song.  If you don't want to bother, just play (C)!

     
